        "function_barriers.dt.title5": "Use Local Values",
        "function_barriers.title": "Function Barriers",
        "in_utility_network.descr": "The utility network that contains the subnetwork to export.",
        "in_utility_network.title": "Input Utility Network",
        "include_barriers.descr": "<xdoc><note type=\"note\"/><p group=\"note\">This parameter is only available for Python.</p></xdoc>",
        "include_barriers.title": "Include Barrier Features",
        "include_domain_descriptions.descr": "<xdoc><p>Specifies whether domain descriptions will be included in the output .json file to communicate domain mapping for controllers, featureElements, connectivity, and associations.<ul><li>Checked—Domain descriptions will be included in the results.</li><li>Unchecked—Domain descriptions will not be included in the results. This is the default.</li></ul></p><note type=\"note\"/><p group=\"note\">For enterprise geodatabases, this parameter requires ArcGIS Enterprise 10.9.1 or later.</p></xdoc>",
        "include_domain_descriptions.title": "Include domain descriptions",
        "include_geometry.descr": "<xdoc><p>Specifies whether geometry will be included in the results.<ul><li>Checked—Geometry will be included in the results.</li><li>Unchecked—Geometry will not be included in the results. This is the default.</li></ul></p><note type=\"note\"/><p group=\"note\">For enterprise geodatabases, this parameter requires ArcGIS Enterprise 10.7 or later.</p></xdoc>",
        "include_geometry.title": "Include geometry",
        "out_json_file.descr": "The name and location of the .json file that will be generated.",
        "out_json_file.title": "Output JSON",
        "out_utility_network.title": "Updated Utility Network",
        "params.category1": "Trace Parameters",
        "propagators.descr": "<xdoc><note type=\"note\"/><p group=\"note\">This parameter is only available for Python.</p></xdoc>",
        "propagators.dt.title1": "Attribute",
        "propagators.dt.title2": "Substitution Attribute",
        "propagators.dt.title3": "Function",
        "propagators.dt.title4": "Operator",
        "propagators.dt.title5": "Value",
        "propagators.title": "Propagators",
        "result_fields.descr": "<xdoc><p>The fields from a feature class that will be returned as results. The values of the fields will be returned in the results for the features in the subnetwork.</p><note type=\"note\"/><p group=\"note\">For enterprise geodatabases, this parameter requires ArcGIS Enterprise 10.7 or later.</p></xdoc>",
        "result_fields.dt.title1": "Feature Class",
        "result_fields.dt.title2": "Field Name",
        "result_fields.title": "Result Fields",
        "result_network_attributes.descr": "<xdoc><p>The network attributes that will be included in the results.</p><note type=\"note\"/><p group=\"note\">For enterprise geodatabases, this parameter requires ArcGIS Enterprise 10.7 or later.</p></xdoc>",
        "result_network_attributes.title": "Result Network Attributes",
        "result_types.descr": "<xdoc><p>Specifies the types of results that will be returned.</p><ul><li><span title=\"CONNECTIVITY\">Connectivity</span>—Features that are connected through geometric coincidence or connectivity associations will be returned. This is the default.</li><li><span title=\"FEATURES\">Features</span>—Feature-level information will be returned.</li><li><span title=\"CONTAINMENT_AND_ATTACHMENT_ASSOCIATIONS\">Containment and attachment associations</span>—Features that are associated through containment and structural attachment associations will be returned.</li></ul><note type=\"note\"/><p group=\"note\">For enterprise geodatabases, this parameter requires ArcGIS Enterprise 10.7 or later.</p><p group=\"note\">The containment and attachment associations option requires ArcGIS Enterprise 10.8.1 or later.</p></xdoc>",
        "result_types.domain.CONNECTIVITY": "Connectivity",
        "result_types.domain.CONTAINMENT_AND_ATTACHMENT_ASSOCIATIONS": "Containment and attachment associations",
        "result_types.domain.FEATURES": "Features",
        "result_types.title": "Result Types",
        "subnetwork_name.descr": "The name of the subnetwork that will be exported from the tier. Select a specific source to export the corresponding subnetwork information. When the subnetworks table contains 10,000 or more records for a tier, the parameter's choice list is not populated and an empty field is provided for the subnetwork name.",
        "subnetwork_name.title": "Subnetwork Name",
        "summary": "<xdoc><p>Exports subnetworks from a utility network into a .json file. This tool also allows you to delete a row in the Subnetworks table as long as the <span class=\"esri_fieldname\">Is deleted</span> attribute is set to true. This indicates that the subnetwork controller has been removed from the subnetwork.</p><note type=\"note\"/><p group=\"note\">Starting with ArcGIS Enterprise 10.9.1, the export subnetwork operation processes asynchronously using the UtilityNetworkTools geoprocessing service when working with a utility network in an enterprise geodatabase. The UtilityNetworkTools service is preconfigured in the System folder for feature services that include a utility network. It has a longer time-out setting and is reserved for utility network geoprocessing tasks.</p></xdoc>",
        "tier.descr": "The tier that contains the subnetwork.",
        "tier.title": "Tier",
        "title": "Export Subnetwork",
        "traversability_scope.descr": "<xdoc><p>Specifies the type of traversability that will be applied. Traversability scope determines whether traversability is applied to junctions, edges, or both. For example, if a condition barrier is defined to stop the trace if DEVICESTATUS is set to Open and traversability scope is set to edges only, the trace will not stop even if the trace encounters an open device, because DEVICESTATUS is only applicable to junctions. In other words, this parameter indicates to the trace whether to ignore junctions, edges, or both.</p><ul><li><span title=\"BOTH_JUNCTIONS_AND_EDGES\">Both junctions and edges</span>—Traversability will be applied to both junctions and edges. This is the default.</li><li><span title=\"JUNCTIONS_ONLY\">Junctions only</span>—Traversability will be applied to junctions only.</li><li><span title=\"EDGES_ONLY\">Edges only</span>—Traversability will be applied to edges only.</li></ul><note type=\"note\"/><p group=\"note\">This parameter is only available for Python.</p></xdoc>",
        "traversability_scope.domain.BOTH_JUNCTIONS_AND_EDGES": "Both junctions and edges",
        "traversability_scope.domain.EDGES_ONLY": "Edges only",
        "traversability_scope.domain.JUNCTIONS_ONLY": "Junctions only",
        "traversability_scope.title": "Apply Traversability To"
    }
}
